        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "6d55084a-700a-5926-95d8-f9346e2a782f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Siege of Salto, Uruguayan War\n- People: Marquis of Tamandaré, Venancio Flores, Bartolomé Mitre\n- Places: Salto, Uruguay, Argentina\n- Organizations: Brazilian forces, Colorado forces, Uruguayan Army\n\nFacts:\n- The Siege of Salto took place during the Uruguayan War from 22 to 28 November 1864.\n- During the Siege of Salto, Brazilian forces under the Marquis of Tamandaré and Colorado forces under Venancio Flores attempted to capture the city of Salto in Uruguay from Uruguayan Army defenders.\n- During the Uruguayan War, Argentina aided Venancio Flores.\n- Argentine president Bartolomé Mitre provided Venancio Flores with supplies, Argentine volunteers, and river transport for troops.",
